  {
    "n": 3,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-blue);\" data-correct=\"C\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"An internal Application Load Balancer resolves only to private IP addresses, so it can be reached solely from inside the VPC. With the tasks in private subnets using awsvpc network mode, each service calls the internal load balancer&#x27;s private DNS name and the traffic never leaves the VPC, which satisfies the security review.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 2: Private service-to-service on ECS&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Deploy the tasks in public subnets with public IP addresses, and restrict the security groups to the service ports.&quot;, &quot;Deploy the tasks in private subnets, and place an internet-facing Application Load Balancer in the public subnets.&quot;, &quot;Deploy the tasks in private subnets, and place an internal Application Load Balancer in the same private subnets.&quot;, &quot;Deploy the tasks in public subnets, and route the traffic between the services through a NAT gateway.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Deploy the tasks in private subnets, and place an internal Application Load Balancer in the same private subnets.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;An internal Application Load Balancer resolves only to private IP addresses, so it can be reached solely from inside the VPC. With the tasks in private subnets using awsvpc network mode, each service calls the internal load balancer&#x27;s private DNS name and the traffic never leaves the VPC, which satisfies the security review.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Assigning public IP addresses places the task network interfaces in a public subnet, so traffic between the services leaves through the internet gateway. Security groups restrict which sources may connect, but they do not keep the traffic inside the VPC.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;An internet-facing load balancer is created in public subnets and resolves to public IP addresses, so a call from one service to another would leave the VPC and come back through the internet gateway. The tasks are private but the path between them is not.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;An internal Application Load Balancer resolves only to private IP addresses, so it can be reached solely from inside the VPC. With the tasks in private subnets using awsvpc network mode, each service calls the internal load balancer&#x27;s private DNS name and the traffic never leaves the VPC, which satisfies the security review.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;A NAT gateway provides outbound internet access for resources in private subnets and cannot accept inbound connections, so it cannot carry traffic from one service to another. Tasks in public subnets do not send traffic through a NAT gateway either.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/application-load-balancers.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/application-load-balancers.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 1 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 2 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 2: Private service-to-service on ECS</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Deploy the tasks in public subnets with public IP addresses, and restrict the security groups to the service ports.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Deploy the tasks in private subnets, and place an internet-facing Application Load Balancer in the public subnets.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Deploy the tasks in private subnets, and place an internal Application Load Balancer in the same private subnets.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Deploy the tasks in public subnets, and route the traffic between the services through a NAT gateway.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 1</div></div>",
