  {
    "n": 4,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-blue);\" data-correct=\"B\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"An IAM role attached to an instance profile provides temporary credentials that are automatically rotated. Scoping the policy to specific resource ARNs follows least privilege. The application can use the AWS SDK to assume the role credentials without storing long-term keys.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 3: Least privilege for EC2&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Create an IAM user with an access key and secret key. Attach policies that allow s3:GetObject and sqs:SendMessage. Store the credentials in the application configuration file.&quot;, &quot;Create an IAM role with a policy that allows s3:GetObject on the specific bucket ARN and sqs:SendMessage on the specific queue ARN. Attach the role to the EC2 instance profile.&quot;, &quot;Create an IAM role with the AmazonS3FullAccess and AmazonSQSFullAccess managed policies. Attach the role to the EC2 instance profile.&quot;, &quot;Create an IAM role with a policy that allows s3:* and sqs:* actions. Add a condition key to restrict access to the current AWS Region only.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Create an IAM role with a policy that allows s3:GetObject on the specific bucket ARN and sqs:SendMessage on the specific queue ARN. Attach the role to the EC2 instance profile.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;An IAM role attached to an instance profile provides temporary credentials that are automatically rotated. Scoping the policy to specific resource ARNs follows least privilege. The application can use the AWS SDK to assume the role credentials without storing long-term keys.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;Storing long-term credentials in application configuration files is a security risk. If the file is compromised or accidentally committed to source control, the credentials are exposed. IAM roles with instance profiles are the recommended approach for EC2-based applications.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;An IAM role attached to an instance profile provides temporary credentials that are automatically rotated. Scoping the policy to specific resource ARNs follows least privilege. The application can use the AWS SDK to assume the role credentials without storing long-term keys.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;Using FullAccess managed policies grants permissions far beyond what the microservice needs. This violates the principle of least privilege. The microservice only needs s3:GetObject and sqs:SendMessage on specific resources, not full access to all S3 and SQS operations across the account.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;Allowing all S3 and SQS actions (s3:* and sqs:*) is overly permissive even with a Region restriction. Least privilege requires specifying only the exact actions needed (s3:GetObject and sqs:SendMessage) and scoping to specific resource ARNs.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 1 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 3 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 3: Least privilege for EC2</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create an IAM user with an access key and secret key. Attach policies that allow s3:GetObject and sqs:SendMessage. Store the credentials in the application configuration file.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create an IAM role with a policy that allows s3:GetObject on the specific bucket ARN and sqs:SendMessage on the specific queue ARN. Attach the role to the EC2 instance profile.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create an IAM role with the AmazonS3FullAccess and AmazonSQSFullAccess managed policies. Attach the role to the EC2 instance profile.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Create an IAM role with a policy that allows s3:* and sqs:* actions. Add a condition key to restrict access to the current AWS Region only.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 1</div></div>",
