  {
    "n": 6,
    "mode": "native",
    "native": "<div class=\"slide-native sm-skill sm-check\" style=\"--accent:var(--aws-blue);\" data-correct=\"C\" data-multi=\"\" data-rationale=\"Route 53 health checks monitor endpoints from multiple geographic locations. The health check results show which regions experience failures and can distinguish between DNS, TCP connection, and HTTP response issues. This provides visibility into whether the problem is DNS resolution, network connectivity, or the application itself.\" data-judge=\"{&quot;prompt&quot;: &quot;Question 5: Is it DNS, the network, or the backend?&quot;, &quot;options&quot;: [&quot;Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query API Gateway access logs for the affected Region.&quot;, &quot;Use AWS X-Ray to trace requests from CloudFront through API Gateway.&quot;, &quot;Use Route 53 health checks to monitor the endpoint and analyze the health check results by Region.&quot;, &quot;Use AWS CloudTrail to review API calls made to Route 53 and CloudFront.&quot;], &quot;answer&quot;: &quot;Use Route 53 health checks to monitor the endpoint and analyze the health check results by Region.&quot;, &quot;why&quot;: &quot;Route 53 health checks monitor endpoints from multiple geographic locations. The health check results show which regions experience failures and can distinguish between DNS, TCP connection, and HTTP response issues. This provides visibility into whether the problem is DNS resolution, network connectivity, or the application itself.&quot;, &quot;explanations&quot;: {&quot;A&quot;: &quot;CloudWatch Logs Insights can analyze API Gateway logs. However, this only shows requests that successfully reached API Gateway. It cannot identify DNS resolution failures or network connectivity issues that prevent requests from reaching the API.&quot;, &quot;B&quot;: &quot;X-Ray traces requests within the application after they reach AWS services. X-Ray cannot diagnose DNS resolution failures or network connectivity issues between end users and AWS edge locations. It only traces requests that successfully reach instrumented services.&quot;, &quot;C&quot;: &quot;Route 53 health checks monitor endpoints from multiple geographic locations. The health check results show which regions experience failures and can distinguish between DNS, TCP connection, and HTTP response issues. This provides visibility into whether the problem is DNS resolution, network connectivity, or the application itself.&quot;, &quot;D&quot;: &quot;CloudTrail records AWS API management calls (such as creating or modifying resources). It does not record end-user data plane requests like DNS queries or content delivery. CloudTrail cannot diagnose connectivity issues experienced by end users.&quot;}, &quot;sources&quot;: [&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover.html&quot;]}\" data-sources=\"[&quot;https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover.html&quot;]\"><div class=\"kicker\">SESSION 1 &middot; KNOWLEDGE CHECK &middot; QUESTION 5 of 5</div><h2>Check yourself <span class=\"sm-check-hint\">click an option</span></h2><p class=\"sm-check-q\">Question 5: Is it DNS, the network, or the backend?</p><div class=\"sm-opts\"><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"A\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">A</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to query API Gateway access logs for the affected Region.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"B\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">B</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Use AWS X-Ray to trace requests from CloudFront through API Gateway.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"C\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">C</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Use Route 53 health checks to monitor the endpoint and analyze the health check results by Region.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button><button class=\"sm-opt\" data-ltr=\"D\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"sm-opt-l\">D</span><span class=\"sm-opt-t\">Use AWS CloudTrail to review API calls made to Route 53 and CloudFront.</span><span class=\"sm-opt-m\"></span></button></div><div class=\"sm-check-fb\" style=\"display:none\"></div><div class=\"sm-source\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-circle-question\"></i> Knowledge check &middot; Content Review Session 1</div></div>",
